// Sundara Kāṇḍa (Book 5) of Gosvāmī Tulasīdāsa's Śrī Rāmacaritamānasa (Awadhi), complete: the three
// opening Sanskrit ślokas, then 60 dohā-groups (the caupāīs before each dohā/sorṭhā, with the chandas
// where they occur, and the dohā itself). Collated Nov 2026; not yet checked line by line against a
// printed edition.
//
// Sources (digital witnesses; a first-hand Gita Press scan or Hindi Wikisource Sundarkāṇḍa could not
// be had: Wikisource has only the Bāla Kāṇḍa, gitapress.org / sanskritdocuments.org / drikpanchang.com
// refused automated access):
//   A. bhaktibharat.com, "Śrī Rāmacaritamānasa: Sundara Kāṇḍa", one page per dohā (pad 1-60) and the
//      maṅgalācaraṇa page: base text. It follows the Gita Press numbering and spelling (मंयका, पुलिस्त,
//      सुह्रद, मुत्यु …), with 60 dohās, (क)/(ख) at 39, 49, 56.
//   B. hindupad.com, "सुंदरकाण्ड": a looser copy with Sanskritised spelling (it also repeats a line in
//      pad 1), so it served only to arbitrate. A and B carry the same Hindi bhāvārtha, so they
//      are probably not independent.
//   C. WirelessAlien/Ramcharitmanas (Unlicense JSON dataset), read through the npm package
//      hindu-devotional-texts 0.7.0 (src/scriptures/sundarkand.ts): 3 ślokas + 60 dohā segments.
// A and C agree word for word except at the places below; the A and C share a few slips (below), so
// they are likely cousins.
// Readings chosen against A:
//   pad 12 रिजटा (A, dropped त्) -> त्रिजटा (B, C; and A itself at pad 11)
//   pad 44 दुष्टहदय (A, C, dropped ृ) -> दुष्टहृदय (B)
//   pad 25 देखउ (A, B) -> देखउँ (first person, C देखेउँ)
// Readings kept from A against a variant:
//   pad 2  आसिष देह गई (A, C) / देइ (B);  pad 3 कनक कोट (A, C) / कोटि (B);  pad 4 बिरंचि / बिरंच (B)
//   pad 6  हठि करिहउँ (A, C) / सठि (B);  pad 23 रिषि पुलिस्त जसु बिमल मंयका (A, C: Gita Press
//   spelling) / पुलस्ति ... मयंका (B);  pad 25 कीन्हिसि (A, B) / कीन्हसि (C);  pad 41 मुत्यु (A, C) /
//   मृत्यु (B);  pad 44 जय कृपाल कहि कपि चले (A, B) / without कपि (C);  pad 48 सुह्रद (A, C) / सुहृद (B);
//   pad 55 कहुँ (A, B) / कहु (C);  pad 56 तव भ्रातहि (A, B) / तब (C);  everywhere else the spelling of
//   ी/ि, ू/ु and the nasals (मै, मों) follows A.
// The reading marked "(A, C)" against B in pad 2, 23 and 41 is the least certain: if a printed
// Gita Press copy reads देइ or मृत्यु, correct here.
// Numbering: all witnesses number the dohās 1-60 alike; none differs. Dohās 39, 49 and 56 each carry
// two couplets, (क) and (ख), kept together under one n. Dohā 12 is a sorṭhā. Chandas: three stanzas
// in 3, two in 35, and the closing stanza in 60 (unnumbered, before dohā 60). The caupāī and chanda
// numbers, and the printed marker "मासपारायण, चौबीसवाँ विश्राम" (after the last chanda), are omitted.
// Layout follows hanuman-chalisa.ts: one pāda per line, ending ' ।' then ' ॥' alternately; the dohā
// as two lines. Totals: 526 caupāī ardhālis (1052 pādas), 62 dohā couplets and 1 sorṭhā couplet
// (60 numbered), 6 chanda stanzas. The colophon line is the last, unnumbered item. Nukta letters are
// written without the dot. English meanings are original; Hindi meanings are in
// src/data/meanings/hi/tulsi-sundar-kand.ts.
// Settled against the Gita Press text on review: pad 2 आसिष देइ गई, pad 23 रिषि पुलस्ति ... मयंका, pad 41
// मृत्यु, and सुहृद (A and C share these slips of typing; B has the printed readings).
