          meaning: { en: 'The ocean said: Lord, Nila and Nala are two monkey brothers who received a sage’s blessing in childhood; by their touch even huge mountains will float across the sea by your power. I too shall keep your majesty in my heart and help according to my strength. In this way, Lord, bridge the sea, so that your fine fame is sung in the three worlds. With this arrow kill the sinful wicked ones living on my northern shore. Hearing the sea’s pain the merciful, calm-in-battle Rama at once took it away. Seeing Rama’s great strength and manhood the ocean became glad and happy; he told the Lord all that had happened, bowed at his feet and went away. The stanza says: the sea went to his own house, and this plan pleased Raghupati. Tulsidas has sung this story, which destroys Kali’s stains, as far as his understanding allows. Raghupati’s qualities are a house of joy, destroyers of doubt, suppressors of sorrow; giving up all hope and reliance on others, sing and hear them always, foolish mind. Singing Raghunayak’s qualities is the giver of all auspiciousness; those who hear it with reverence cross the ocean of existence without a boat.' },
